@startuml activity-pdf-deck-detection
'' PlantUML over Mermaid because deck detection is an ordered rule table (first match wins) run on evidence
'' gathered in parallel, followed by a second decision (which layout to mount in) — a decision-centric control
'' flow whose steps belong to four different owners. PlantUML activity swimlanes show the owner of each step,
'' fork/end fork shows the parallel evidence and page measure, and `elseif` chains render the rules in their
'' exact order; the fills come from the shared theme and the SVG renders byte-reproducibly (README §4). Lanes and
'' fills, from the shared palette: teal = the renderer's pdf.js engine (renderer.pdf);
'' orange = the pure, process-agnostic deck model (vinary.slides.*), the "model orange" of the pure libraries;
'' blue = re-frame + DataScript (:pdf/deck-detected → :doc/deck); blue-violet = the app-db inputs of the layout.
!include _vv-theme.iuml
!pragma useVerticalIf on

title Deck detection and the layout a PDF opens in (ADR-0045)

|#E3F2ED|renderer · pdf.js engine (renderer.pdf)|
start
:the PDF's bytes: the byte cache's newest version
(a CANDIDATE from vv:content, else the last good one);  <<RENDERER_TINT>>
:**prepare!** — pdf.js getDocument (a copy of the bytes),
leased through the warm cache;  <<RENDERER_TINT>>
fork
  :**page-sizes** — every page's size at scale 1
  (in parallel with the evidence: Promise.all),
  the measure the layout needs anyway;  <<RENDERER_TINT>>
fork again
  :**vinary.slides.evidence/gather** — getMetadata
  (Info Creator and Producer, XMP CreatorTool) ·
  getPageMode · getPageLabels. Each call is caught
  on its own: a failure is nil, never a failed open;  <<IR_TINT>>
end fork
|#F5EAE0|pure deck model (vinary.slides.*)|
:**deck/classify** the evidence and the sizes —
<latex>n</latex> is the page count, <latex>s</latex> the common size when
every page agrees within <latex>0.5\,\mathrm{bp}</latex> (uniform);  <<IR_TINT>>
if (Creator or CreatorTool matches \\bbeamer\\b (any case)\nand (<latex>n \ge 2</latex>, or one page of a Beamer paper,\nor one doubled for a second screen)?) then (yes)
  :deck · **definite** · :beamer;  <<IR_TINT>>
elseif (/PageMode is FullScreen\n(ISO 32000-1 §7.7.2)?) then (yes)
  :deck · **definite** · :fullscreen-mode;  <<IR_TINT>>
elseif (<latex>n \ge 2</latex>, uniform, and <latex>s</latex> is a slide tool's\nexport canvas (960 × 540, 720 × 405, …)?) then (yes)
  :deck · **probable** · :slide-export;  <<IR_TINT>>
elseif (<latex>n \ge 2</latex>, uniform, <latex>s</latex> a Beamer paper or one doubled,\nand the Producer is a TeX engine?) then (yes)
  :deck · **probable** · :beamer-geometry;  <<IR_TINT>>
else (no rule matched)
  :not a deck — landscape pages
  alone never qualify;  <<IR_TINT>>
endif
:second-screen axis: does <latex>s</latex> double a Beamer paper
in width (:horizontal) or height (:vertical)?;  <<IR_TINT>>
if (a Beamer source (:beamer, :beamer-geometry),\nno second-screen axis, one label per page?) then (yes)
  :**frames-from-labels** — a frame is a maximal run
  of ADJACENT pages sharing one non-blank label;  <<IR_TINT>>
else (no)
  :one frame per page (one XeLaTeX pass writes no labels,
  a two-screen deck's labels are corrupt);  <<IR_TINT>>
endif
|#E3F2ED|renderer · pdf.js engine (renderer.pdf)|
:the artifact **{:doc :sizes :deck}** — no extra I/O:
the same calls serve a local, sftp://, archive or web PDF;  <<RENDERER_TINT>>
|#E2EBF3|re-frame + DataScript|
:pdf-view dispatches [:pdf/deck-detected path stamp summary]
→ :doc/deck {:deck? :tier :source :pages :frame-count
:second-screen}, written only when it changed;  <<REFRAME_TINT>>
|#E3E7F2|app-db: the layout request|
:deck/effective-layout over [:ui :presentation],
the view's :pdf-layout and :slides-open-as;  <<APPDB_TINT>>
if (presenting?) then (yes)
  :Slides layout;  <<APPDB_TINT>>
elseif (this document view's explicit\nchoice (:pdf-layout)?) then (yes)
  :that layout;  <<APPDB_TINT>>
elseif (a deck, and :slides-open-as\nis not :document?) then (yes)
  :Slides layout;  <<APPDB_TINT>>
else (no)
  :Document layout;  <<APPDB_TINT>>
endif
|#E3F2ED|renderer · pdf.js engine (renderer.pdf)|
:**mount-prepared!** in that layout — the FIRST mount
already has it, so a deck never flashes as a document;  <<RENDERER_TINT>>
stop

legend right
  |= Colour |= Swimlane / concept |
  |<#2D9574>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| renderer: the pdf.js engine (renderer.pdf) |
  |<#E67E22>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| the pure deck model (vinary.slides.deck / .evidence) — the model orange |
  |<#4F97D7>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| re-frame event → DataScript :doc/deck |
  |<#7590DB>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| app-db inputs of the layout choice |
  Rules are tried in order; the first that matches decides. The tier is
  informational: both tiers open as slides.
endlegend
@enduml
